        <h2>About Isaac Newton</h2>
        <p><i>(4 January 1643 – 31 March 1727) was an English polymath, physicist, mathematician, and astronomer who laid the
        foundation for classical mechanics.</i></p>
        <h3>Early life and Education</h3>
        <p>Sir Isaac Newton was born in the 4th January 1643 in Woolsthorpe, Lincolnshire, England, 
            shortly after his father's death.He enterd Trinity college in cambridge
        in 1661 earning his <mark>Bachelors degree</mark> in 1665</p>
        <h3>His early breakthrough discoveries</h3>
        <p>Published Philosophiæ Naturalis Principia Mathematica (1687), formulating the three laws of
        motion and the law of universal gravitation.Aswell as that ,he Proved that <del>black</del> white light is a mix of colored rays using a prism and built the first practical reflecting telescope.</p>
        <h4>Later Life and Legacy</h4>
        <p>Sir Isaac Newton spent his later years in London transitioning from an isolated academic into a powerful public official
        and cultural icon. Moving to the capital in 1696, he became Master of the Royal Mint, where he aggressively prosecuted
        counterfeiters and oversaw the Great Recoinage, while also serving as President of the Royal Society from 1703 until his
        death and earning a knighthood from Queen Anne in 1705. Alongside intense private studies in alchemy and theology, as
        well as a bitter priority dispute with Gottfried Wilhelm Leibniz over calculus, Newton's legacy was cemented by his
        foundational laws of motion, universal gravitation, and optics. His mathematical approach to nature sparked the
        Enlightenment, shaped modern physics for over two centuries, and earned him a grand burial in Westminster Abbey
        following his death in 1727.</p>

